  "assessment": {
    "tokenizer": "Both tokenizer candidates passed the unchanged full local gate. 200 microseconds gained 0.192% and 2 milliseconds gained 0.270% over fresh control 26949, both below 1%. Their margin over the older 26766 native-runtime observation is negative (-0.161% and -0.083%). Do not call either a new best or attribute a causal tokenizer gain from one run per setting.",
    "prefill_flashinfer": "Job 27077 passed the same local gate but delivered 6.365% less good output throughput than matched control 26949. Mean/p95 ITL improved (14.499/14.659 ms vs 14.979/15.147 ms), while mean/p95 TTFT worsened (1480/1886 ms vs 1128/1423 ms). This is a throughput/latency tradeoff in one run, not a whole-system improvement or a causal best.",
    "other_observations": "All four runs had zero profiling errors/cancellations, 7/8 smoke with no regression, 12/12 retrieval and no selected transport errors or tracebacks in role logs. The tokenizer arms have 26 TTFT breaches and zero ITL breaches each; FlashInfer has 30 TTFT breaches and zero ITL breaches. These remain within the unchanged joint >=90% request gate. All three server roles, rank-local queue/running/token gauges, GPU activity and sampled VRAM, host CPU/memory and HTTP/error polls are recorded in per-run review JSON. Telemetry is sparse five-second sampling within request-start envelope; it omits warmup/final drain, has uncalibrated host clock skew, and is not causal evidence. Official full-set accuracy is UNKNOWN; request IDs are not actual model token IDs."
